    "introduction": "Tritax Big Box REIT owns and develops large logistics properties in the UK, providing space used by retailers, manufacturers and distribution businesses. Its operating assets generate rent, while its land and development activities create opportunities for additional buildings and future income. The business focuses on properties suited to modern supply chains and generally seeks durable tenant relationships. Returns depend on occupancy, lease terms, rental growth and changes in property values. Development requires capital and successful delivery before rent begins. Access to transport and power infrastructure can affect site appeal, while interest rates and financing costs influence the economics of its property investments.",
